  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x?$",
  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/9aa292639642f664a81078a5cf916a7f7efef4f4b4a944a85c17bfc63b11beb8.png)\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/f7c2d23d12059c5fe56ce44757825e6c95517e842caeded02b734bbfdc5f7945.png)",
